    <string name="menu_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_how_heading">How it was made</string>
    <string name="about_how_1">Warden-Gambits is a native Android game written in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, with no graphics engine: here the logic rules. Beneath the cards beats a pure, deterministic combo-combat engine, tuned with a simulator that plays thousands of adventures to balance the numbers.</string>
    <string name="about_how_2">The story is written as data (24 zones and 507 nodes on the road to Mordor), the map is generated by code, the sounds are synthesised and the pixel-art images were made with Gemini from the author’s own prompts. It was all built with AI assistance (Claude Code), following a workflow of specs, plans, tests and reviews.</string>
    <string name="about_author_heading">The author</string>
    <string name="about_author_body">Oscar Martínez Gómez is a programmer, a lover of Tolkien’s world and a retired player of The Lord of the Rings Online (LOTRO). There, playing the Warden and its gambits, combos chained blow by blow, the idea for this game was born.</string>
    <string name="about_source_heading">Source code</string>
    <string name="about_source_body">The game’s source code is public: you can read it, learn from it or suggest improvements on GitHub.</string>
